From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make device residency sets resident per command buffer

STEAMAC-3/D8/D9 (1.9.15, M4, macOS 15.7.3, appid 1043240): SIGABRT
`_addResidencySets:387: failed assertion` in -[IOGPUMetalCommandQueue
addResidencySet:] <- MVKQueue::initMTLCommandQueue <- MVKDevice::initQueues
<- vkCreateDevice. Metal allows 32 residency sets per MTLCommandQueue.
MoltenVK caches its MTLCommandQueues per physical device (they are scarce),
shares them between all VkDevices, and added each VkDevice's residency set
to the shared queue, so the 33rd VkDevice alive at once aborted the process.

Attach the device's residency set to each Metal command buffer MVKQueue
creates (useResidencySet:, macOS 15) instead of to the shared queue; remove
the queue add/remove path. Every command buffer that encodes device work is
created by MVKQueue::getMTLCommandBuffer; the device's deferred-release
fence buffers encode nothing.

Regression: REPRO_CASE=queue-residency host/moltenvk/repro/run.sh <libdir>:
40 VkDevices alive on one physical device each fill and read back their own
buffer, then half are replaced and all submit again. The 1.9.15 MoltenVK
aborts creating device 33 ("command queue residency set limit of 32
exceeded"); with this patch all pass.

Generated-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.h b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.h
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.h
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKDevice.h
@@ -1026,18 +1026,18 @@
 	}
 #endif
 
-	void addResidencySet(id<MTLCommandQueue> queue) {
+	/**
+	 * Makes this device's residency set resident for the command buffer. Metal allows only
+	 * 32 residency sets per MTLCommandQueue, and MTLCommandQueues are cached per physical device
+	 * and shared by every VkDevice, so adding each device's set to the queue aborted the process
+	 * at the 33rd live VkDevice (STEAMAC-3/D8/D9: _addResidencySets failed assertion).
+	 */
+	void useResidencySet(id<MTLCommandBuffer> mtlCmdBuff) {
 #if MVK_XCODE_16
-		if (_residencySet) [queue addResidencySet:_residencySet];
+		if (_residencySet && mtlCmdBuff) [mtlCmdBuff useResidencySet:_residencySet];
 #endif
 	}
 
-	void removeResidencySet(id<MTLCommandQueue> queue) {
-#if MVK_XCODE_16
-		if (_residencySet) [queue removeResidencySet:_residencySet];
-#endif
-	}
-
 	bool hasResidencySet() {
 #if MVK_XCODE_16
 		return _residencySet != nil;
diff --git a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKQueue.mm b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKQueue.mm
--- a/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKQueue.mm
+++ b/MoltenVK/MoltenVK/GPUObjects/MVKQueue.mm
@@ -174,6 +174,8 @@
 	}
 	mtlCmdBuff = [_mtlQueue commandBufferWithDescriptor: mtlCmdBuffDesc];
 	[mtlCmdBuffDesc release];														// temp release
+	// The device's allocations, per command buffer: the queue is shared by every VkDevice (STEAMAC-3)
+	_device->useResidencySet(mtlCmdBuff);
 
 	addPerformanceInterval(getPerformanceStats().queue.retrieveMTLCommandBuffer, startTime);
 	NSString* mtlCmdBuffLabel = getMTLCommandBufferLabel(cmdUse);
@@ -332,7 +334,6 @@
 // Retrieves and initializes the Metal command queue and Xcode GPU capture scopes
 void MVKQueue::initMTLCommandQueue() {
 	_mtlQueue = _queueFamily->getMTLCommandQueue(_index);	// not retained (cached in queue family)
-	_device->addResidencySet(_mtlQueue);
 
 	_submissionCaptureScope = new MVKGPUCaptureScope(this);
 	if (_queueFamily->getIndex() == getMVKConfig().defaultGPUCaptureScopeQueueFamilyIndex &&
@@ -346,7 +347,6 @@
 MVKQueue::~MVKQueue() {
 	destroyExecQueue();
 	_submissionCaptureScope->destroy();
-	_device->removeResidencySet(_mtlQueue);
 
 	[_mtlCmdBuffLabelBeginCommandBuffer release];
 	[_mtlCmdBuffLabelQueueSubmit release];
